  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Application Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the user\'s request for a local web app that merges round sticker PDFs into A4 sheets. I\'m focusing on the core requirements of client-side PDF handling, image selection, and sheet merging using HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JavaScript. I am carefully considering the technical feasibility of each component.\n\n\n**Clarifying Technical Approach**\n\nI\'m now determining the most effective architecture. While the initial request implied a vanilla JavaScript approach, the provided project structure is a React SPA using Vite, Tailwind CSS, and other dependencies. I\'m focusing on leveraging this environment for better structure. I\'m choosing to implement the functionality within the React SPA framework rather than attempting a conflicting vanilla approach, which seems like a cleaner, safer, and better approach.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Intent**\n\nI\'ve honed in on the absolute priority: respecting user intent. Given the React environment, I\'m building a React 18+ component with Vite. It will provide the functionality the user requested. My current plan is to mock the sticker data in order to show a responsive React component.\n\n\n**Refining Dummy Data Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data strategies. How do we get sticker PDFs to the user? Providing a dummy `stickers.json` library, but without actual files, has me thinking: Let\'s create dummy PDF data! I can either provide 5 styled dummy files, generate data, *or* let users upload custom stickers. Better yet, dynamically generate them using `pdf-lib` and canvas! This elegant solution can embed rendered stickers with user data into the A4 PDF.\n\n\n**Evaluating User Request Details**\n\nI\'ve got it! The user *does* specify file selection via a `stickers.json` file. The UI will have a \"Library\" column and a \"Selection\" column. \"Genereer A4 PDF\" generates the merged PDF using `pdf-lib`. A dynamic, A4-sized PDF will render a fixed grid with clicked stickers. I need to make a UI grid and a way to calculate A4 PDF coordinates.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 112637720
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
