  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing the Library**\n\nI\'ve made great strides! The library excels at retrieving `stickers.json`, gracefully handling failures. It allows custom sticker PDF uploads, converting them to `Uint8Array`, and prompts for names and colors, saving them into the relevant format. This is an exciting milestone!\n\n\n**Constructing the Preview**\n\nI\'m now focused on the interactive A4 sheet preview. I\'m building `/src/components/PreviewSheet.tsx` to visualize the sticker layout, maintaining the correct aspect ratio (1:1.414). I intend for this component to dynamically render grid layouts based on user-defined rows, columns, margins, and spacing, with visual indicators for sticker slots, and the capacity to render empty, dashed slots. This visual tool should provide an excellent, pixel-perfect preview for the user.\n\n\n**Mapping the Grid**\n\nI\'ve transitioned to the visual grid mapping process within `/src/components/PreviewSheet.tsx`. The core challenge is translating the flat sticker list into a visual grid layout. I\'ve devised a flattening strategy based on `selectedItems`, using a nested loop for quantity. This flattened list then drives the grid rendering logic. I\'m focusing on handling both filled and empty slots, displaying stickers as circles with icons and titles, and empty slots as dashed borders. I\'m taking responsive design principles into account, storing and updating dimensions in state, rather than using fixed calculations, based on container size changes.\n\n\n**Refining the Preview**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a pure CSS/SVG-based preview, leveraging `aspect-ratio` for perfect A4 dimensions! Tailwind\'s native support makes this a breeze. My focus is on rendering the page within the aspect ratio container, using percentage-based calculations relative to the page width for margins, widths, and gaps. This offers a simple and responsive solution, translating all `mm` dimensions into percentages! The inline styles can use CSS variables to compute positioning.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 18
      nanos: 600308458
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
